[2026-09-21 12:43:29 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP AUDIT]   Audit: Post-2017 cometary discovery footprint vs OSSOS TNO footprint.
[2026-09-21 12:43:29 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP AUDIT]   This audit evaluates the sky-coverage geometry and discovery locations of
[2026-09-21 12:43:29 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP AUDIT]   post-2017 long-period comets (Pan-STARRS, ATLAS, ZTF, Catalina, etc.) in
[2026-09-21 12:43:29 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP AUDIT]   contrast to the OSSOS characterized survey footprint.
[2026-09-21 12:43:29 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP AUDIT]   Specifically:
[2026-09-21 12:43:29 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP AUDIT]   1. Extract first-observation coordinates (RA, Dec, obstime, observatory)
[2026-09-21 12:43:29 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP AUDIT]   for all post-2017 C/ comets.
[2026-09-21 12:43:29 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP AUDIT]   2. Compute their ecliptic coordinates (lambda_disc, beta_disc) and solar
[2026-09-21 12:43:29 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP AUDIT]   elongation at discovery.
[2026-09-21 12:43:29 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP AUDIT]   3. Test whether cometary discoveries cluster in ecliptic longitude, and
[2026-09-21 12:43:29 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP AUDIT]   measure their angular distance to:
[2026-09-21 12:43:29 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP AUDIT]   - Declared transit axis (34 deg, -13 deg)
[2026-09-21 12:43:29 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP AUDIT]   - Displaced systematic axis (120 deg, -40 deg)
[2026-09-21 12:43:29 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP AUDIT]   4. Compare this cometary discovery footprint against the OSSOS survey blocks
[2026-09-21 12:43:29 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP AUDIT]   (which are targeted TNO pointings, not all-sky comet searches).
[2026-09-21 12:43:29 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP AUDIT]   Outputs
[2026-09-21 12:43:29 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP AUDIT]   results/audits/audit_post2017_discovery_footprint.json
